# Single Player campaign path from launch to the first mission's combat, for the native client
# (sfcop --input; oracle/driver/run_native.sh --steps). analysis/campaign/README.md is the finding
# this file reproduces.
#
# Coordinates are the game's display pixels (an 800x600 display, the same space as
# oracle/driver/skirmish.steps). Calibrated on the native build, 2026-11-07, with --shots captures
# of each screen: Select Game -> Single Player -> Campaign Selector -> New Campaign (Federation) ->
# the campaign's opening slides -> the campaign map, recentred -> one sector down -> Missions ->
# Patrol -> Mission Briefing -> READY -> combat.
#
# The campaign is not the same from run to run (the ship's name and the sectors' contents are
# drawn from the clock), and the map opens either on the player's sector or on its top-left
# corner; the compass clicks below put the player's sector at the centre of the map view in both
# cases, and moving one sector away offers a Patrol mission. A mouse moved over the window
# during a windowed run can scroll the map away from that sector (the map scrolls at its edges):
# leave the window alone, or run headless.

window 120 Starfleet Command
sleep 50000

# --- main menu, "Select Game": SINGLE PLAYER opens the Single Player screen
click 237 232
sleep 8000

# --- Single Player: CAMPAIGN opens the Campaign Selector (the saved campaigns)
click 618 191
sleep 8000

# --- Campaign Selector: NEW GAME opens New Campaign
click 398 445
sleep 8000

# --- New Campaign: Federation (third row of the list), then BEGIN NEW CAMPAIGN. The game then
# reads every mission module a second time (MissionSpecEntry) before the slides come up.
click 128 201
sleep 2000
click 617 440
sleep 40000

# --- the campaign's opening slides, CLICK TO CONTINUE; a click left over lands on the map's text
# panel and does nothing
click 400 550
sleep 4000
click 400 550
sleep 4000
click 400 550
sleep 4000
click 400 550
sleep 4000
click 400 550
sleep 4000
click 400 550
sleep 4000
click 400 550
sleep 4000
click 400 550
sleep 6000

# --- the map opens either on the player's sector or on its top-left corner. The compass
# scrolls one sector per click and stops at the map's edge: north and west until the corner,
# then six sectors south and eleven east puts the player's sector back at the centre.
click 712 118
sleep 2000
click 712 118
sleep 2000
click 712 118
sleep 2000
click 712 118
sleep 2000
click 712 118
sleep 2000
click 712 118
sleep 2000
click 712 118
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 685 145
sleep 2000
click 712 172
sleep 2000
click 712 172
sleep 2000
click 712 172
sleep 2000
click 712 172
sleep 2000
click 712 172
sleep 2000
click 712 172
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
click 737 145
sleep 2000
sleep 3000

# --- the campaign map: the player's sector is at (412, 275); the one below it is (412, 365).
# The ship moves there over the next game days, and MISSIONS lights up.
click 412 365
sleep 40000

# --- MISSIONS opens the Mission Selector with one row, Patrol; ACCEPT loads its module and opens
# the Mission Briefing
click 48 277
sleep 12000
click 547 203
sleep 10000

# --- Mission Briefing: READY starts the mission (the module is loaded again for the tactical game)
click 598 501
sleep 60000
